: ASM_ARCH=x86_64_nasm_gnu,x86_64_nasm_macho :
: BLOCK_TEST :
: RUN_ASM :

:/
Expected: storing 2147483648u64 through ptr u64 preserves all 64 bits.
The x86_64 GNU backend currently stores 0xFFFFFFFF80000000 by emitting
MOV qword [ptr], 2147483648. A qword memory store sign-extends its imm32 operand.
The local initializer is zero to isolate this store from initialization.
/:
@[inline(never)]
function write482(ptr u64 target) -> i0 {
    dref target = 2147483648u64;
}

start() {
    u64 value = 0;
    write482(ref value);
    if value != 2147483648u64; { exit 1; }
    exit 42;
}

:/ OUTPUT
@exit_code=42
/:
